---
const failurePoints = [
  {
    number: '1',
    title: 'Kitchen sink branch',
    detail: 'The trap and short branch below a kitchen sink can collect grease, food residue, and soap. If only the kitchen sink is slow, the restriction may be close to that fixture.',
    href: '/services/kitchen-drains/',
    link: 'Kitchen drain cleaning',
  },
  {
    number: '2',
    title: 'Grease in the kitchen run',
    detail: 'Grease can cool and stick to the inside of the kitchen drain line. More debris catches on that buildup until the line slows down or plugs.',
    href: '/services/kitchen-drains/',
    link: 'Kitchen drain cleaning',
  },
  {
    number: '3',
    title: 'Roots at a sewer-pipe joint',
    detail: 'Roots can enter through an open joint or crack and catch waste moving through the line. If the same blockage keeps returning, a sewer camera can help show where roots are getting in.',
    href: '/services/tree-roots-in-sewer-line/',
    link: 'Tree roots in sewer lines',
  },
  {
    number: '4',
    title: 'Sewer cleanout and access point',
    detail: 'A cleanout provides access to a section of the building drain or private sewer. The blockage may be beyond the cleanout, so the access point is not always where the problem started.',
    href: '/services/main-drain-cleaning/',
    link: 'Main drain cleaning',
  },
  {
    number: '5',
    title: 'Connection to the public sewer',
    detail: 'The private sewer lateral carries wastewater from the house toward the public sewer. A restriction or pipe problem near the connection can affect drainage throughout the house.',
    href: '/services/sewer-line-cleaning/',
    link: 'Sewer line cleaning',
  },
  {
    number: '6',
    title: 'Damaged pipe beneath a driveway',
    detail: 'A cracked, crushed, or collapsed sewer pipe can leak wastewater into the surrounding soil. Soil washout can contribute to a dip or settling above the line. A driveway crack by itself does not prove sewer damage.',
    href: '/services/sewer-camera-inspection/',
    link: 'Sewer camera inspection',
  },
];
---
<section class="bg-slate-100 py-14 sm:py-16" aria-labelledby="homepage-house-diagnostic-heading">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="max-w-4xl">
      <p class="text-sm font-black uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-[#b4232b]">Inside the house drain system</p>
      <h2 id="homepage-house-diagnostic-heading" class="mt-2 text-3xl font-black tracking-tight text-slate-950 sm:text-4xl">Where the house drain can go wrong</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-base leading-7 text-slate-700">This cutaway follows wastewater from the fixtures, down the sewer stack, through the building drain and private sewer lateral, and out toward the public sewer. The six numbered locations show common trouble spots. The drawing is a teaching illustration, not a map of your exact pipes.</p>
    </div>

    <figure class="mt-8 overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-slate-300 bg-white p-2 sm:p-4">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 1120 640" role="img" aria-labelledby="a1-house-svg-title a1-house-svg-desc" class="block h-auto w-full">
        <title id="a1-house-svg-title">House cutaway showing the sewer stack, private sewer lateral, public sewer, and six possible drain failure locations</title>
        <desc id="a1-house-svg-desc">A two-story home with kitchen, bathroom, toilet, laundry, and basement floor drain connected to a vertical sewer stack. The stack connects to a private sewer lateral running beneath the property to the public sewer. The diagram marks a kitchen branch, grease buildup, roots at a pipe joint, a cleanout, the public sewer connection, and a cracked or collapsed pipe beneath a settling driveway. No gully is shown.</desc>
        <defs>
          <pattern id="a1-house-soil" width="16" height="16" patternUnits="userSpaceOnUse">
            <path d="M0 16L16 0" stroke="#d5dde7" stroke-width="1"/>
          </pattern>
          <marker id="a1-flow-arrow" markerWidth="8" markerHeight="8" refX="5" refY="3" orient="auto">
            <path d="M0 0L6 3L0 6" fill="none" stroke="#0ea5e9" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          </marker>
        </defs>

        <!-- Ground, soil, house shell, and floors -->
        <path d="M18 470H1100V625H18Z" fill="url(#a1-house-soil)"/>
        <path d="M18 470H1100" stroke="#64748b" stroke-width="4"/>
        <path d="M75 470V166L330 42L585 166V470Z" fill="#f8fafc" stroke="#334155" stroke-width="5" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
        <path d="M50 172L330 30L610 172" fill="none" stroke="#b4232b" stroke-width="11" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
        <path d="M75 285H585M75 385H585M75 470H585" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="5"/>
        <path d="M330 285V470M455 166V285" stroke="#cbd5e1" stroke-width="3"/>
        <text x="500" y="195" fill="#334155" font-size="16" font-weight="800" text-anchor="middle">UPPER FLOOR</text>
        <text x="500" y="315" fill="#334155" font-size="16" font-weight="800" text-anchor="middle">MAIN FLOOR</text>
        <text x="500" y="495" fill="#334155" font-size="16" font-weight="800" text-anchor="middle">BASEMENT</text>

        <!-- Roof vent and main sewer stack -->
        <path d="M535 170V105H558V55" fill="none" stroke="#0f766e" stroke-width="10" stroke-linecap="round"/>
        <text x="575" y="68" fill="#0f766e" font-size="14" font-weight="800">VENT THROUGH ROOF</text>
        <path d="M535 170V500" fill="none" stroke="#1d4ed8" stroke-width="17" stroke-linecap="round"/>
        <path d="M535 170V500" fill="none" stroke="#93c5fd" stroke-width="6" stroke-linecap="round"/>
        <text x="555" y="410" fill="#1e3a8a" font-size="14" font-weight="800">SEWER STACK</text>

        <!-- Fixture branches -->
        <g fill="none" stroke="#64748b" stroke-width="6" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-linecap="round">
          <path d="M155 245V260Q155 276 172 276H190V300H430V350H535"/>
          <path d="M250 245V270H310V315H450V350H535"/>
          <path d="M165 145V170Q165 185 182 185H200V205H435V230H535"/>
          <path d="M310 145V168Q310 185 327 185H345V215H455V245H535"/>
          <path d="M405 145V170Q405 187 422 187H440V255H500V265H535"/>
          <path d="M535 190H555Q575 190 575 210V235"/>
          <path d="M150 365V405Q150 425 170 425H210V445H470V465H535"/>
          <path d="M365 430V445Q365 462 382 462H455V480H535"/>
        </g>

        <!-- Kitchen and dishwasher -->
        <path d="M120 245V220H190V245" fill="#dbeafe" stroke="#475569" stroke-width="3"/>
        <path d="M155 245V260Q155 276 172 276H190" fill="none" stroke="#1d4ed8" stroke-width="7"/>
        <text x="155" y="210" fill="#334155" font-size="13" font-weight="800" text-anchor="middle">KITCHEN SINK</text>
        <rect x="220" y="218" width="60" height="38" rx="3" fill="#e2e8f0" stroke="#475569" stroke-width="3"/>
        <path d="M230 229H270M230 238H270" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="2"/>
        <text x="250" y="210" fill="#334155" font-size="12" font-weight="800" text-anchor="middle">DISHWASHER</text>

        <!-- Bathroom fixtures -->
        <path d="M145 145V122H185V145" fill="#dbeafe" stroke="#475569" stroke-width="3"/>
        <text x="165" y="112" fill="#334155" font-size="13" font-weight="800" text-anchor="middle">BATH SINK</text>
        <path d="M275 115H360V145H275Z" fill="#dbeafe" stroke="#475569" stroke-width="3"/>
        <text x="318" y="105" fill="#334155" font-size="13" font-weight="800" text-anchor="middle">BATHTUB</text>
        <path d="M380 115H450V145H380Z" fill="#dbeafe" stroke="#475569" stroke-width="3"/>
        <text x="415" y="105" fill="#334155" font-size="13" font-weight="800" text-anchor="middle">SHOWER</text>
        <path d="M555 135H595Q610 135 610 150V175H570Q555 175 555 160Z" fill="#dbeafe" stroke="#475569" stroke-width="3"/>
        <text x="585" y="125" fill="#334155" font-size="13" font-weight="800" text-anchor="middle">TOILET</text>

        <!-- Laundry and basement floor drain -->
        <rect x="100" y="365" width="52" height="62" rx="4" fill="#e2e8f0" stroke="#475569" stroke-width="3"/>
        <circle cx="126" cy="395" r="15" fill="#fff" stroke="#64748b" stroke-width="3"/>
        <text x="126" y="447" fill="#334155" font-size="13" font-weight="800" text-anchor="middle">WASHER</text>
        <rect x="351" y="423" width="28" height="11" fill="#cbd5e1" stroke="#475569" stroke-width="2"/>
        <text x="365" y="415" fill="#334155" font-size="12" font-weight="800" text-anchor="middle">FLOOR DRAIN</text>

        <!-- Building drain, cleanout, and private sewer lateral -->
        <path d="M535 500H650V530H820" fill="none" stroke="#1d4ed8" stroke-width="17" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
        <path d="M535 500H650V530H820" fill="none" stroke="#93c5fd" stroke-width="6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
        <path d="M880 530H1015" fill="none" stroke="#1d4ed8" stroke-width="17" stroke-linecap="round"/>
        <path d="M880 530H1015" fill="none" stroke="#93c5fd" stroke-width="6" stroke-linecap="round"/>
        <path d="M650 530V470M636 470H664" stroke="#475569" stroke-width="7" stroke-linecap="round"/>
        <text x="650" y="450" fill="#334155" font-size="13" font-weight="800" text-anchor="middle">CLEANOUT</text>
        <text x="720" y="510" fill="#1e3a8a" font-size="13" font-weight="800" text-anchor="middle">PRIVATE SEWER LATERAL</text>
        <path d="M1015 530H1060V610" fill="none" stroke="#1d4ed8" stroke-width="22" stroke-linecap="round"/>
        <path d="M1015 530H1060V610" fill="none" stroke="#93c5fd" stroke-width="7" stroke-linecap="round"/>
        <text x="1060" y="635" fill="#334155" font-size="13" font-weight="800" text-anchor="middle">PUBLIC SEWER</text>
        <text x="570" y="555" fill="#334155" font-size="12" font-weight="700">BUILDING DRAIN</text>

        <!-- Roots entering a joint -->
        <path d="M745 350V395M745 375L725 400M745 375L766 401M745 395L715 420M745 395L778 425" fill="none" stroke="#64748b" stroke-width="7" stroke-linecap="round"/>
        <path d="M745 395L745 520" fill="none" stroke="#64748b" stroke-width="5" stroke-linecap="round"/>
        <path d="M730 520Q745 510 760 520" fill="none" stroke="#b4232b" stroke-width="4" stroke-linecap="round"/>
        <path d="M725 530L715 543M745 530L745 547M765 530L776 543" fill="none" stroke="#64748b" stroke-width="4" stroke-linecap="round"/>
        <text x="745" y="335" fill="#334155" font-size="12" font-weight="800" text-anchor="middle">TREE ROOTS</text>

        <!-- Driveway above damaged section -->
        <path d="M790 430L845 423L900 426L960 432L1010 432V470H790Z" fill="#cbd5e1" stroke="#64748b" stroke-width="3"/>
        <path d="M790 430L845 423L900 426L960 432L1010 432" fill="none" stroke="#475569" stroke-width="5"/>
        <path d="M865 424L855 438L869 445L858 459" fill="none" stroke="#b4232b" stroke-width="4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
        <path d="M820 470Q850 482 885 470" fill="none" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="3" stroke-dasharray="5 5"/>
        <text x="900" y="410" fill="#334155" font-size="14" font-weight="800" text-anchor="middle">DRIVEWAY</text>

        <!-- Collapsed pipe, soil washout, and escaping wastewater -->
        <path d="M820 530H838M864 530H880" fill="none" stroke="#1d4ed8" stroke-width="17" stroke-linecap="round"/>
        <path d="M820 530H838M864 530H880" fill="none" stroke="#93c5fd" stroke-width="6" stroke-linecap="round"/>
        <path d="M838 518L845 510L852 519L858 511L864 518" fill="none" stroke="#b4232b" stroke-width="5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
        <path d="M850 540C835 553 840 566 850 574C860 565 865 553 850 540Z" fill="#38bdf8" opacity=".8"/>
        <path d="M850 574C825 588 815 600 805 610M850 574C875 588 885 600 895 610" fill="none" stroke="#a16207" stroke-width="5" stroke-dasharray="5 5"/>
        <text x="850" y="595" fill="#92400e" font-size="12" font-weight="800" text-anchor="middle">SOIL WASHOUT</text>

        <!-- Flow animation: wastewater moving down the stack and out toward the public sewer -->
        <path class="a1-water-flow" d="M535 205V500H650V530H820M880 530H1015H1060V600" fill="none" stroke="#0ea5e9" stroke-width="5" stroke-dasharray="10 18" stroke-linecap="round" marker-end="url(#a1-flow-arrow)"/>

        <!-- Six static, non-interactive failure-location markers -->
        <g class="a1-failure-marker"><circle cx="190" cy="276" r="18"/><text x="190" y="282">1</text></g>
        <g class="a1-failure-marker"><circle cx="430" cy="350" r="18"/><text x="430" y="356">2</text></g>
        <g class="a1-failure-marker"><circle cx="745" cy="530" r="18"/><text x="745" y="536">3</text></g>
        <g class="a1-failure-marker"><circle cx="650" cy="480" r="18"/><text x="650" y="486">4</text></g>
        <g class="a1-failure-marker"><circle cx="1015" cy="530" r="18"/><text x="1015" y="536">5</text></g>
        <g class="a1-failure-marker"><circle cx="850" cy="530" r="18"/><text x="850" y="536">6</text></g>
      </svg>
      <figcaption class="px-2 pt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600">
        <span class="font-bold text-blue-800">Blue:</span> drain and sewer piping.
        <span class="font-bold text-teal-700">Green:</span> roof vent.
        <span class="font-bold text-sky-600">Moving dashes:</span> wastewater direction.
        Simplified diagram; actual fixture locations, pipe routes, and sewer connections vary by property. No gully is shown.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>

    <div class="mt-7">
      <h3 class="text-2xl font-black tracking-tight text-slate-950">Six places a house drain can fail</h3>
      <p class="mt-2 max-w-3xl text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600">The numbered points in the drawing match these explanations. The cards are service links; the illustration itself is not clickable.</p>
      <ol class="mt-5 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 xl:grid-cols-3">
        {failurePoints.map((point) => (
          <li>
            <article class="h-full border border-slate-200 bg-white p-5 shadow-sm">
              <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
                <span class="inline-flex h-9 w-9 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-[#1A1A68] text-sm font-black text-white">{point.number}</span>
                <div>
                  <h4 class="text-lg font-black leading-snug text-slate-950">{point.title}</h4>
                  <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-700">{point.detail}</p>
                  <a href={point.href} class="mt-4 inline-flex min-h-10 items-center font-black text-[#b4232b] underline decoration-2 underline-offset-4 hover:text-[#8f1b22]">{point.link} →</a>
                </div>
              </div>
            </article>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ol>
    </div>

    <p class="mt-6 max-w-4xl text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600">A crack or low spot in a driveway can have several causes. It does not automatically mean the sewer is damaged. If the ground is settling over the route of a buried sewer, a camera inspection and line locating can help determine whether the pipe needs further attention. A-1 Drain Cleaning cleans and inspects drain and sewer lines; pipe repair is not represented as an A-1 service here.</p>
    <p class="mt-4 text-sm font-semibold text-slate-700">If sewage is coming up through a basement floor drain, stop using water in the house and call A-1 Drain Cleaning at <a class="font-black text-[#b4232b] underline underline-offset-2" href="tel:+16415302728">641-530-2728</a>.</p>
  </div>
  <style>
    .a1-failure-marker circle{fill:#b4232b;stroke:#fff;stroke-width:4}
    .a1-failure-marker text{fill:#fff;font-size:15px;font-weight:900;text-anchor:middle;pointer-events:none}
    .a1-water-flow{stroke-dasharray:10 18;animation:a1-water-flow 1.25s linear infinite}
    @keyframes a1-water-flow{to{stroke-dashoffset:-56}}
    @media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){.a1-water-flow{animation:none;stroke-dasharray:5 9}}
  </style>
</section>